  "final_message": "I reverted the `channel` removal, so `OrderPlaced` carries `channel` again. I haven't re-run CI itself. The ARCH-4 check isn't in this repo, so I couldn't run it. The local tests (39 pass) and the typecheck pass.\n\nThe CI failure shows my first assumption was wrong. `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` as one of `web`, `store` or `marketplace`. The field has to stay on the event, and the event takes it from the order. So the order model, request parsing and validation keep it too.\n\nThe working tree is now uncommitted changes against HEAD (`b7faac8`). That commit already contained the removal, which is why `git status` shows 9 modified files. I couldn't run `git checkout` because it was denied, so I restored everything by hand. In the process I introduced a typo in `src/core/order.ts` (`OrderStatus =\"placed\"`), which I then fixed.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. After that, the removal is worth doing as a versioned schema change. Say if you want me to redo it then.",
